[BEGIN]
  ObjTp=Hd
  Cmn1=EtherGate Preset v1.0\\\\Presets for the Channel rows registered||1
  Cmn2=on the selected EtherGate.\\The gateway does not store presets.||1
  Cmn3=This module does.\\\\Eight rows. Each row is one preset button.\\
  Cmn4=Preset, Preset_No, and Preset_FB share that row.\\AllWithAny keeps||1
  Cmn5=those three together.\\\\Preset replaces Recall and Save. From the||1
  Cmn6=rising edge, in 0.1s steps:\\  Press high                  Preset_FB||1
  Cmn7=high, until a blink\\  release before Hold_Time    recall\\  hold||1
  Cmn8=for Hold_Time          save, then blink Preset_FB\\  still held||1
  Cmn9=at 10s           erase\\\\Hold_Time is how long the press must be||1
  Cmn10=held to save.\\Default 2.5s, range 0.5s to 9.0s. Time or ticks.||1
  Cmn11=1t = 0.01s.\\Confirmation_Time is the total save blink, shared by||1
  Cmn12=every row.\\\\Preset_No on the row is which stored preset that button||1
  Cmn13=uses.\\0 is off, and that row does nothing. 1 through 64 select||1
  Cmn14=that preset.\\Preset_Trigger recalls any of those 64 by number,||1
  Cmn15=using this symbol's\\fade and channel list. 0 does nothing. It does||1
  Cmn16=not save or erase.\\Return it to 0 before sending the same number||1
  Cmn17=again.\\Preset_Save stores any of those 64 by number, using this||1
  Cmn18=symbol's\\channel list. 0 does nothing. It does not recall or erase.
  Cmn19=\\Return it to 0 before sending the same number again.\\A value||1
  Cmn20=present at startup waits until the analog changes.\\\\Fade_Time||1
  Cmn21=is seconds on the symbol (0.5s is half a second, 0 is\\a cut). Fade_Time_Override
  Cmn22=||1is tenths of a second. It is ignored\\until an analog value arrives.
  Cmn23=||1After that, the analog is the fade,\\and 0 is a cut. 5 is 0.5 seconds.
  Cmn24=||150 is 5.0 seconds.\\\\Channels is the comma-separated list this||1
  Cmn25=symbol controls.\\Empty means every defined channel. 12 is channel||1
  Cmn26=12 on either\\port. 1:12 is port 1 channel 12, and 2:12 is port||1
  Cmn27=2. Spaces\\around commas are ignored. A token that is not a channel||1
  Cmn28=is\\skipped. 255 characters.\\Channels_Override$ is ignored until||1
  Cmn29=a string arrives. After that,\\the serial is the list, and an empty||1
  Cmn30=serial means every channel.\\Save with a list writes those channels||1
  Cmn31=and leaves the others\\stored. Recall moves only stored channels||1
  Cmn32=in the list. A 10s\\hold removes those channels. An empty list saves||1
  Cmn33=every defined\\channel, replacing the preset, and a 10s hold clears||1
  Cmn34=it.\\\\Controller_Override is ignored until an analog value arrives.
  Cmn35=||1After that,\\1-8 selects that slot.
[END]
